  "features": [
    "Complete UI/UX overhaul for the 800x480 5-inch touch display, designed as a dedicated field instrument rather than a scaled-down desktop app",
    "One authoritative UI layer (pph6_ui.py): older UI modules no longer build any page, own navigation, or draw any widget - backend hooks (measurement engine, access point controller, update checker) are used directly",
    "Reusable component system: header/status chip, metric cards, action buttons, persistent bottom nav, list rows, progress bars, page indicator, modal overlay, notification toasts",
    "Centralized animation manager with FULL/REDUCED/OFF levels, per-page cancellation, slide page transitions, animated boot sequence, animated connection flow, value interpolation",
    "Access Point pairing code, SSID, password and LAN IP all directly visible with no submenu",
    "Fixes a live production crash in 5.2.2 (scanline() called without self, binding a color string as the Tk parent) by fully replacing the affected UI layer",
    "Verified end-to-end with tools/ui_smoke_test.py plus manual Xvfb screenshot review of all 28 pages, including a caught-and-fixed card-visibility z-order bug, three self.X() AttributeError bugs, a falsy-zero bug hiding valid 0% packet loss, a German-locale free(1) parsing bug, and a sliding-bottom-nav violation of the spec"
  ],
